{"id":"G12-I1","variant":"*","board":"*","template":"T01","screen":"N.5","title":"Income rises: three markets","currency":"£","model":{"vars":[["f_hol","1+2*inc/100"],["d_hol","2*inc"],["f_milk","1+0.5*inc/100"],["d_milk","0.5*inc"],["f_bus","1+-1*inc/100"],["d_bus","-1*inc"]]},"controls":[{"id":"inc","type":"range","label":"Income change","min":-10,"max":10,"start":0,"step":2,"fmt":"{spct(v)}"}],"panels":[{"type":"xy","x":{"label":"Quantity","min":0,"max":150},"y":{"label":"Price (£)","min":0,"max":12},"els":[{"t":"fn","x":"10*(12-y)","k":"grey","lab":"D1","dash":true,"if":"inc!=0"},{"t":"fn","x":"10*(12-y)*f_hol","k":"d","lab":"{inc==0 ? \"D\" : \"D2\"}"},{"t":"hline","y":6,"k":"grey","dash":"3 4"},{"t":"drop","x":"60*f_hol","y":6,"xl":"{fmt(60*f_hol,0)}","yl":"£6"}],"h":200,"title":"Holidays abroad (a luxury): YED +2"},{"type":"xy","x":{"label":"Quantity","min":0,"max":150},"y":{"label":"Price (£)","min":0,"max":12},"els":[{"t":"fn","x":"10*(12-y)","k":"grey","lab":"D1","dash":true,"if":"inc!=0"},{"t":"fn","x":"10*(12-y)*f_milk","k":"d","lab":"{inc==0 ? \"D\" : \"D2\"}"},{"t":"hline","y":6,"k":"grey","dash":"3 4"},{"t":"drop","x":"60*f_milk","y":6,"xl":"{fmt(60*f_milk,0)}","yl":"£6"}],"h":200,"title":"Milk (a necessity): YED +0.5"},{"type":"xy","x":{"label":"Quantity","min":0,"max":150},"y":{"label":"Price (£)","min":0,"max":12},"els":[{"t":"fn","x":"10*(12-y)","k":"grey","lab":"D1","dash":true,"if":"inc!=0"},{"t":"fn","x":"10*(12-y)*f_bus","k":"d","lab":"{inc==0 ? \"D\" : \"D2\"}"},{"t":"hline","y":6,"k":"grey","dash":"3 4"},{"t":"drop","x":"60*f_bus","y":6,"xl":"{fmt(60*f_bus,0)}","yl":"£6"}],"h":200,"title":"Bus journeys (an inferior good): YED −1"}],"readouts":[{"l":"Holidays abroad","v":"{spct(d_hol)}","k":"blue"},{"l":"Milk","v":"{spct(d_milk,1)}","k":"blue"},{"l":"Bus journeys","v":"{spct(d_bus)}","k":"blue"}],"predict":{"q":"Incomes rise by 10%. What happens on the bus journeys diagram?","options":[{"k":"A","s":"Demand shifts right","fb":"That is what happens to normal goods. Bus journeys here have negative YED: richer people drive instead."},{"k":"B","s":"Demand shifts left","fb":"Bus journeys are an inferior good (YED −1): a 10% rise in income cuts demand by 10% at every price."},{"k":"C","s":"A movement along the demand curve","fb":"A movement along the curve needs a change in the good's own price. Income shifts the curve."},{"k":"D","s":"No change, because the price of a bus journey has not changed","fb":"Price has not changed, but income has. Income is a cause of shifts in demand."}],"correct":"B"},"task":"Move the **income** slider to +10%, then to −10%, and watch all three demand curves.","target":{"expr":"inc==10","do":"Move the income slider to +10%, then press Check."},"takeaway":"Income changes **shift** demand: right for normal goods (furthest for luxuries), left for inferior goods.","explore":"At −10%: holidays −20%, milk −5%, bus journeys +10%.","alt":"Income rises: three markets","test":{"set":{"inc":10},"expect":["near(d_bus,-10)","near(d_hol,20)","near(d_milk,5)"],"cases":[{"set":{"inc":-10},"expect":["near(d_bus,10)","near(d_hol,-20)","near(d_milk,-5)"]}]}}